# Line endings (2026-11-02, docs/claude/2026-11-02-legacy-cleanup.md; unified 2026-11-17 for the overhaul, see
# docs/claude/2026-11-16-wiring-rewrite-plan.md section 八 item 4).
# Default: text is stored and checked out with LF on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says. This keeps
# pinned source hashes (scripts/*-discovery.mjs, smoke harness) identical on a Windows clone.
# On 2026-11-17 the 63 source, test, style and doc files that still had CRLF or mixed endings were converted to LF, so a
# Claude editing them no longer breaks a file's endings. New files: LF. Only the files below keep their exact bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Preserve reviewed upstream bytes so source ZIPs match the pinned asset hashes.
assets/bundled/** -text
# Windows launchers and scripts keep CRLF regardless of checkout settings.
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
# Pinned by hash (scripts/lib/smoke-isolation.mjs LOCATOR_SHA256): converting it means re-reviewing and re-pinning.
electron/safety/codex.ts -text
# Archived copies keep the bytes they were archived with.
docs/archive/** -text
